<article class="env-lemma" id="0GJ8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GJ8">Lemma <span data-tag="0GJ8">59.75.7</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism of schemes. Let $K \in D^+(X_{\acute{e}tale})$. Let $\overline{s}$ be a geometric point of $S$ and let $\overline{t}$ be a geometric point of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}^{sh}_{S, \overline{s}})$. We have a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ (Rf_*K)_{\overline{s}} \ar[r]_{sp} \ar@{=}[d] &  (Rf_*K)_{\overline{t}} \ar@{=}[d] \\  R\Gamma (X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}^{sh}_{S, \overline{s}}), K) \ar[r] &  R\Gamma (X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}^{sh}_{S, \overline{t}}), K) }  \]
</div>
  <p> where the bottom horizontal arrow arises as pullback by the morphism $\text{id}_ X \times c$ where $c : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}^{sh}_{S, \overline{t}}) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}^{sh}_{S, \overline{s}})$ is the morphism introduced in Remark <a href="/tag/0GJ4" data-tag="0GJ4">59.75.2</a>. The vertical arrows are given by Theorem <a href="/tag/03Q9" data-tag="03Q9">59.53.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from the description of $sp$ in Remark <a href="/tag/0GJ4" data-tag="0GJ4">59.75.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>